The MATLAB files in the code/ directory perform the main processing and analysis steps used in the study.

lazer_windows_create36_preproces.m

This script creates 36-sample laser windows from the preprocessed laser signal. The window-based representation is used to capture local temporal variations in the laser photon-count sequence.

acoustic_import_8_avgchannel.m

This script imports the eight-channel acoustic chirp recordings and converts them into a single-channel representation by averaging the eight channels.

laser_acoustic_dataset_create.m

This script extracts features from both laser and acoustic signals and creates the combined laser-acoustic dataset. Laser and acoustic features are calculated separately and then prepared for fusion.

laser_acoustic_data_fusion.m

This script performs early feature-level fusion by combining laser-derived and acoustic-derived features into a single fused feature vector.

acoustic_channel_graph.m

This script generates graphical representations of the acoustic channel data and the averaged acoustic signal.

evaluation_pca.m

This script performs Principal Component Analysis (PCA) on the fused feature dataset and generates the PCA-based explained variance analysis.

evaluation_corelation_matrix.m

This script calculates and visualizes the correlation matrix of the extracted fused features.
